# Build output. `build/` is deliberately NOT ignored: the release workflow ships
# build/<name> as an artifact, so it is tracked.
/target
*.pdb

# The frozen Rust oracle's build tree (~3 GB). rust-old/ itself is tracked --
# it is the parity oracle, see docs/development/roadmap.md 3.6.0.
rust-old/target/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/

# --- Retired 2026-08-26 (3.3.1), Rust-era rules that no longer apply ---
# `*.csv`      shadowed benches/history.csv, so the benchmark history could never
#              be committed -- which defeats the cross-commit regression tracking
#              docs/benchmarks.md states as its purpose. That file is now tracked.
# `Cargo.lock` rust-old/Cargo.lock is part of the frozen oracle and IS tracked;
#              the rule only ever created confusion about that.
# `**/*.rs.bk` rustfmt backup files; there is no rustfmt here.
# `/coverage/` tarpaulin output; there is no coverage tooling here.
